OL,3,GNEWSAAnalysis: Nesbitt's departure
OL,4,Aproves politics can't be removed from
OL,5,Ahealth
OL,6,
OL,7,FIn March he told Stormont's health
OL,8,Fcommittee that if he ever felt that his
OL,9,Fparty was trying to influence how he
OL,10,Fdid his role he'd rather "walk or
OL,11,Fresign rather than become some sort of
OL,12,Flap dog or functionary for a political
OL,13,Fparty".
OL,15,FNesbitt has kept to his word.
